WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:09.090
Homophones sound the same, but mean different things.

2
00:00:11.067 --> 00:00:13.946
sea and see sound exactly the same.

3
00:00:15.933 --> 00:00:17.558
The sea is full of water.

4
00:00:19.533 --> 00:00:20.880
You see with your eyes.

5
00:00:21.867 --> 00:00:24.746
The spelling tells the reader which one you mean.

6
00:00:26.733 --> 00:00:28.869
The trickiest ones: there, their, they're.

7
00:00:36.467 --> 00:00:39.439
there is a PLACE. It has 'here' inside it!

8
00:00:45.433 --> 00:00:47.569
their means it BELONGS to them.

9
00:00:48.567 --> 00:00:51.400
It has an 'i' in it. I own things!

10
00:00:55.367 --> 00:00:57.735
they're is two words squeezed together.

11
00:01:05.233 --> 00:01:07.601
they're is short for THEY ARE.

12
00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:12.733
Test: say 'they are'. If it makes sense, use they're.

13
00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:16.325
Next: two, too and to.

14
00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:26.058
two is the NUMBER 2. Think of twins and twice.

15
00:01:32.033 --> 00:01:35.609
too means TOO MUCH or ALSO. It has an extra o!

16
00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:43.665
to is for everything else, like going to a place.

17
00:01:45.633 --> 00:01:47.351
Last one: your and you're.

18
00:01:51.333 --> 00:01:53.376
your means it BELONGS to you.

19
00:01:56.367 --> 00:01:57.992
you're is short for YOU ARE.

20
00:01:59.967 --> 00:02:03.868
Test: 'Is this you are coat?' No! So use your.

21
00:02:05.867 --> 00:02:09.304
'You are my best friend.' Yes! So use you're.

22
00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:17.244
If the long way makes sense, keep the apostrophe.

23
00:02:19.233 --> 00:02:21.787
Your turn! Fill the gaps. Pause the video.

24
00:02:33.767 --> 00:02:35.207
They're equals they are.

25
00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:38.918
two equals the number 2.

26
00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:42.943
your equals it belongs to you.

27
00:02:43.933 --> 00:02:45.280
How many did you get?

28
00:02:51.767 --> 00:02:54.553
Same sound. Check the meaning, then spell it.
